# Initializer & Bootstrap Rule

This rule documents the conventions and responsibilities of the Initializer Module in the Mozome Flutter project.

## Scope

- Applies to: `initializer/`, `main.dart`, dependency injection setup, and environment configuration.

## Purpose

- The Initializer Module is responsible for:
  - Bootstrapping the application.
  - Setting up dependency injection (DI) containers.
  - Loading environment-specific configuration.
  - Ensuring all modules (App, Domain, Data, Shared, Resources) are properly initialized before app launch.

## Structure

- **initializer/lib/src/di/**: Contains DI setup and registration logic.
- **main.dart**: Entry point that calls the initializer before running the app.
- **App Initializer**: Central class/function that orchestrates setup (DI, config, etc).

## Best Practices

- **Centralize all initialization logic** in the Initializer Module.
- **Do not run app logic** (UI, data fetching, etc.) before initialization is complete.
- **Register all dependencies** (repositories, services, mappers, etc.) in the DI container.
- **Load environment variables/config** before initializing services that depend on them.
- **Log initialization steps** for easier debugging.

## Example

```dart
Future<void> main() async {
  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  await AppInitializer.init(); // Sets up DI, config, etc.
  runApp(MyApp());
}
```

